# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tsan job in ci-c.yml. Policy (enforced by
# eng/check-race-suppressions.sh):
# - Third-party code only. Never SDK code.
# - race: entries name a third-party global variable, never a function:
#   TSan matches a function name anywhere in either stack, and Paho's threads
#   call into the SDK (callbacks), so a function entry could hide an SDK race.
# - Only globals in tsan_reviewed (eng/check-race-suppressions.sh), and no
#   substring of SDK code: TSan matches patterns as substrings.
# - Each entry follows a comment giving the upstream file:line and, for Paho,
#   the PAHO_C_TAG it was checked against. Re-check on every tag bump.

# Paho MQTTAsync.c:684 and MQTTAsyncUtils.c:1842,2438 (v1.3.16): written by
# MQTTAsync_connect/MQTTAsync_stop, read by the send thread, no common lock.
race:MQTTAsync_tostop

# Paho MQTTAsync.c:687 and MQTTAsyncUtils.c:1839-1865 (v1.3.16): written by
# MQTTAsync_connect and the send thread without a common lock.
race:sendThread_state

# Paho MQTTAsync.c:1013 (v1.3.16): read by MQTTAsync_inCallback without a
# lock; the send thread writes it (MQTTAsyncUtils.c:1840,1866).
race:sendThread_id

# Paho MQTTAsync.c:1013 (v1.3.16): as above; the receive thread writes it
# (MQTTAsyncUtils.c:2080,2390).
race:receiveThread_id
